# Agent CLI versions pinned into the `claude` and `all` image targets (PA-64,
# reworked by PA-104).
#
# One file, read by `docker/build.sh` and by CI (PA-65), so bumping a pin is a
# one-line change in one place rather than an edit to a Dockerfile plus an edit
# to a pipeline. The Dockerfile itself declares these as ARGs with no defaults
# and fails the build when one is empty, which is what keeps this file
# authoritative instead of merely advisory.
#
# Since PA-104 the image installs every agent with its vendor's *official*
# installer, not npm, so a pin exists only where that installer accepts a
# version. `agent-install.test.ts` fails if this file pins an agent whose
# installer cannot take one, or misses one whose installer can. Settings
# (PA-68) no longer pins anything: every agent updates itself, so an install
# from the UI takes the vendor's current release.
#
# These pins set the version an image *starts* with. They are not meant to be
# current, and an agent that updates itself at run time writes the update into
# the mounted $HOME, which outranks the baked-in copy (see the Dockerfile).
#
# The numbers are the vendors' release numbers, which they also publish to npm
# — which is why renovate.json can still read them from the npm registry even
# though nothing is installed from it.

# https://claude.ai/install.sh <VERSION>  (== @anthropic-ai/claude-code on npm)
CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.274

# https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh --release <VERSION>  (== @openai/codex)
CODEX_VERSION=0.154.0

# https://opencode.ai/install --version <VERSION>  (== opencode-ai)
OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.31

# Deliberately unpinned, because their official installers cannot install a
# specific version — the `all` target takes their current release:
#   agy  https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh  (latest from its manifest)
#   pi   https://pi.dev/install.sh                  (latest from pi.dev's API)

# Not an agent: the headless browser tooling in the `all` target. Pinned
# because the CLI bundles its own playwright-core, and the Chromium revision the
# image installs is whichever that bundled copy expects.
# npm install -g @playwright/cli@<VERSION>
PLAYWRIGHT_CLI_VERSION=0.1.22
